<header><p class="st-kicker">county · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">County of Portugal</h1><p class="st-meta">868 CE – 1139 CE (approx.) · capital Guimarães</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The county of Portucale between the Minho and Douro, founded with the capture of Porto in 868, from which the Kingdom of Portugal was born.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 868 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vimara-peres">Vímara Peres</a>, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-iii-of-asturias">Alfonso III of Asturias</a>, took the town of Portucale (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porto">Porto</a>) on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/douro">Douro</a> and was made count of the region between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minho-river">Minho</a> and the Douro. His descendants governed it as a frontier county within the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-leon">Kingdom of León</a>, and Countess <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mumadona-dias">Mumadona Dias</a> fortified <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guimaraes">Guimarães</a> in the 10th century.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The counts ruled a mixed population of Galician-speaking peasants, resettled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mozarabs">Mozarabs</a> and frontier warriors. The county was abolished after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garcia-ii-of-galicia">García II of Galicia</a> defeated Count <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuno-mendes">Nuno Mendes</a> in 1071. In 1096 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-vi-of-castile">Alfonso VI</a> of León recreated it, now including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coimbra">Coimbra</a>, for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-count-of-portugal">Henry of Burgundy</a>, husband of his daughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teresa-countess-of-portugal">Teresa</a>, who ruled after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-henry-the-navigator">Henry's</a> death in 1112.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teresa-countess-of-portugal">Teresa</a>'s son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afonso-i-of-portugal">Afonso Henriques</a> defeated her party at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sao-mamede">São Mamede</a> in 1128. After his victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ourique">Ourique</a> in 1139 he took the title of king, recognised by León in 1143, and the county became the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-portugal">Kingdom of Portugal</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/county-of-portugal.jpg" alt="County of Portugal" width="320" height="484"><figcaption>Image: Basilio · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Condado_portucalense_carte-1070-fr.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>868 CE – 1139 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>county</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Guimarães</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Vímara Peres, Henry of Burgundy, Teresa</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Galician-Portuguese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/portugal">Portugal</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Condado Portucalense, Portucale</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1004&amp;focus=county-of-portugal" aria-label="County of Portugal on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4478 700 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where County of Portugal lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4798 956L4859 895M4798 956L4865 919M4798 956L4794 911M4798 956L4773 1045"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4859 895h0M4865 919h0M4794 911h0M4773 1045h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4798 956h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4798 956h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Guimarães. <a href="/atlas?year=1004&amp;focus=county-of-portugal">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
